<title>USA: Air Liquide buys Texas Instrument unit.</title>
<headline>Air Liquide buys Texas Instrument unit.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Air Liquide America Corp said Friday it will purchase the chemical operations department of Texas Instruments Inc, subject to regulatory approval.</p>
<p>Terms of the transaction, which the company expects to close before May, were not disclosed.</p>
<p>At the completion of the transaction, the company said about 200 Texas Instrument employees will work for Air Liquide.</p>
<p>The company said the sale builds on the successful partnership between Air Liquide America and Texas Instruments, which have done business for almost 20 years.</p>
</text>
